WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:09.103
"Now is the time," Ally thought as she and Mateo walked to the park to meet Kate and Bethany.

2
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:14.904
"As soon as I see Kate, I'm going to tell her the truth about my phone."

3
00:00:14.905 --> 00:00:22.757
But when they found the girls, Kate was so excited about her T-shirt design, Ally didn't want to interrupt her.

4
00:00:22.758 --> 00:00:25.738
"See?" Kate held out her tablet.

5
00:00:25.739 --> 00:00:33.262
"It's a soccer ball that's been kicked high up into the atmosphere and is circling the sun—like a planet."

6
00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:36.602
"Isn't it stellar?" Bethany asked.

7
00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:40.289
"It's amazing," Ally said.

8
00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:46.111
"Can we add the words Sandville Soccer Club on the back of the shirts?" Mateo asked.

9
00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:53.057
"Sure," Kate said. "And I'll make the letter o in Soccer Club look like a soccer ball."

10
00:00:53.058 --> 00:00:58.236
"Can you send the design to me? I'll send it to the print shop," Mateo said.

11
00:00:58.237 --> 00:01:07.357
"Sure." Kate made some quick changes to the design and sent it to Mateo.

12
00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:13.764
"These T-shirts are going to sell like hotcakes!" Mateo said as he forwarded the design to Eli.

13
00:01:13.765 --> 00:01:20.908
Ally frowned. "I hope they sell better than that! Pancakes are not one of the diner's top sellers."

14
00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:24.391
Mateo, Bethany, and Kate laughed.

15
00:01:24.392 --> 00:01:27.603
"You're so funny, Ally!" Kate said.

16
00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:33.291
"I have the best surprise for you. I bet you'll never guess what happened."

17
00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:37.598
Bethany grinned. "You'll never guess!"

18
00:01:37.599 --> 00:01:39.895
"What happened?" Ally asked.

19
00:01:39.896 --> 00:01:43.192
"No, you have to guess," Kate said.

20
00:01:43.193 --> 00:01:47.846
"I thought you said I'd never guess." Ally was confused.

21
00:01:47.847 --> 00:01:53.475
"Never is a very long time. It's almost as infinite as the universe."

22
00:01:53.476 --> 00:01:56.957
It was Kate and Bethany's turn to be confused.

23
00:01:56.958 --> 00:02:01.793
"Maybe you should just tell us, Kate," Mateo said quickly.

24
00:02:01.794 --> 00:02:05.316
"I found your phone!" Kate cried.

25
00:02:05.317 --> 00:02:10.395
"You did?" Ally blinked in surprise and touched her back pocket.

26
00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:15.149
Alpha was safely tucked away there. And luckily, she was staying quiet.

27
00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.939
"Tell her how it happened, Kate," Bethany said.

28
00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:26.056
Kate pulled an old phone that looked exactly like Alpha from her bag.

29
00:02:26.057 --> 00:02:28.496
"I was putting up signs near the diner.

30
00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:33.317
When I looked down, I spotted the phone just lying on the ground.

31
00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:35.828
It must have fallen out of your pocket one day.

32
00:02:35.829 --> 00:02:41.487
If it wasn't so old, someone else would have picked it up. Here you go!"

33
00:02:41.488 --> 00:02:48.720
"Gosh, thanks so much." Ally flushed. How could she explain her fib now?

34
00:02:48.721 --> 00:02:53.611
"Power it up. Make sure it still works," Bethany said.

35
00:02:53.612 --> 00:02:58.729
"I hope it does. I love the funny things it says!" Kate grinned.

36
00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:05.257
Ally gulped and pressed the Power button. The device lit up instantly.

37
00:03:05.258 --> 00:03:09.584
"What do you think it will say first?" Kate asked eagerly.

38
00:03:09.585 --> 00:03:13.980
"Um . . . er . . . ," Ally fumbled for words.

39
00:03:13.981 --> 00:03:15.932
"I don't think this phone is working—"

40
00:03:15.933 --> 00:03:18.860
"Of course I'm working!" Alpha blurted out.

41
00:03:18.861 --> 00:03:25.777
"Wow!" Kate laughed. "That app is amazing.

42
00:03:25.778 --> 00:03:29.704
The voice sounds like it's coming from your back pocket."

43
00:03:29.705 --> 00:03:35.437
"Ha-ha! Really?" Ally reached around to her back pocket to try to turn Alpha off.

44
00:03:35.438 --> 00:03:39.328
But as Ally pulled her out, Alpha fell to the ground.

45
00:03:39.329 --> 00:03:44.686
"Oh no!" Ally thought, looking down in horror.

46
00:03:44.687 --> 00:03:50.170
"Wait, you have your phone?" Kate frowned.

47
00:03:50.171 --> 00:03:56.941
"I, uh, didn't want to tell you, but I, well, I . . . bought another phone."

48
00:03:56.942 --> 00:04:01.601
As soon as the words came out of her mouth, Ally wanted to take them back.

49
00:04:01.602 --> 00:04:04.519
She had just told another fib!

50
00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:10.916
"You did?" Kate asked. "Why? I told you I'd help you find your old phone."

51
00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.240
"I know," Ally said in a rush.

52
00:04:13.241 --> 00:04:18.152
"But I didn't want to bother you. And besides, the old one isn't working so well."

53
00:04:18.153 --> 00:04:23.838
"I'm working just fine!" Alpha snapped. "I can't believe you replaced me!"

54
00:04:23.839 --> 00:04:27.173
Kate and Bethany cracked up, laughing.

55
00:04:27.174 --> 00:04:31.907
But Ally wanted to cry. "This is awful," she thought.

56
00:04:31.908 --> 00:04:36.470
"My little fibs are spiraling out of control!"

57
00:04:36.471 --> 00:04:41.074
"Oh, look at the time!" Mateo said, quickly checking his phone.

58
00:04:41.075 --> 00:04:44.000
"Ally and I have to get home to help my dad with something.

59
00:04:44.001 --> 00:04:48.571
Thanks again for the design, Kate!"

60
00:04:48.572 --> 00:04:51.639
As they hurried away, Ally looked at him.

61
00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.684
"What do we need to help Ray with?"

62
00:04:53.685 --> 00:04:56.553
"Nothing," Mateo said.

63
00:04:56.554 --> 00:05:01.139
"I just said that as an excuse to get away before things got worse."

64
00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:06.255
Ally blinked. "You mean, you told a fib?"

65
00:05:06.256 --> 00:05:11.795
"I guess." Mateo shrugged. "It was harmless, and you needed help.

66
00:05:11.796 --> 00:05:14.583
No one was going to get hurt because I said it."

67
00:05:14.584 --> 00:05:21.534
Ally shook her head. "So, on Earth it's okay to tell a fib if it doesn't hurt anyone?"

68
00:05:21.535 --> 00:05:24.164
"Yep," Mateo said.

69
00:05:24.165 --> 00:05:27.585
"Phew!" Relief washed over Ally.

70
00:05:27.586 --> 00:05:35.768
"That's great news!" Now she didn't have to tell Kate the truth!

